<p>Russia and Ukraine resumed strikes after a three-day ceasefire expired at midnight Tuesday, with Ukrainian officials saying Russian attacks in Dnipropetrovsk region killed at least six people. Officials said a drone hit an apartment building in Kryvyi Rih, killing two people and injuring four, including a nine-month-old girl, while an aerial bomb strike northeast of the city killed four others and injured three. Russia&#x27;s Defence Ministry said its air defenses destroyed 27 Ukrainian fixed-wing drones over Belgorod, Voronezh and Rostov regions after the truce ended. Ukrainian officials said Russia launched more than 200 drones overnight, damaging energy facilities, apartment buildings, a kindergarten and a civilian locomotive, with debris from a downed drone setting fire to the roof of a 16-storey residential building in Kyiv&#x27;s Obolon district. Zelenskyy said Ukrainian forces struck gas facilities in Russia&#x27;s Orenburg region more than 1,500 km from Ukraine&#x27;s border, and Ukraine&#x27;s military said it also hit Russian targets in occupied Donetsk region after the renewed attacks.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/jOrkCZ2_kR7up4F47mD3OMRBoSlNM4qJ_0ONFkrrYvg4t7ea1CO376BJJ3hBIewTq-INP6umU1wwIwWmz_6PfOie3NEgcCBtqi3bG1wdGlQu' alt='Debris lies around an apartment building hit by a Russian missile and drone strike.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Local toll details: Current Time cited officials as saying the two people killed in Kryvyi Rih were a 43-year-old man and a 65-year-old woman, and that a 23-year-old woman was hospitalized.</li><li>Regional spread: Two people were hurt in Cherkasy region, and officials also reported damage in Zhytomyr and Chernihiv regions after the overnight strikes.</li><li>Defense planning: Zelenskyy said Kyiv was working with European allies on technologies to defend against ballistic missiles.</li><li>Drone mix: Ukrainian figures cited by Privatbankar said the barrage included both strike drones and decoy drones.</li></ul><blockquote>After the end of the partial three-day ceasefire, Russia continues to kill and maim Ukrainians and pressure on it must therefore in no way be weakened - Volodymyr Zelenskyy</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Volodymyr Zelenskyy, Ukraine&#x27;s president: Zelenskyy said fighting continued during the final hours of the truce and that Ukraine had recorded activity along the front, arguing the pause had not fully held even before it expired. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1999789/russia-ukraine-resume-strikes-as-truce-expires'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Russian Defence Ministry: The ministry said air defenses intercepted fixed-wing UAVs over Russian border and southern regions after the ceasefire expired. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1999789/russia-ukraine-resume-strikes-as-truce-expires'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Kyiv military administration: Tymur Tkachenko, head of the capital&#x27;s military administration, said enemy UAVs were over Kyiv during the post-truce attack. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1999789/russia-ukraine-resume-strikes-as-truce-expires'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Kremlin: The Kremlin said it was too early to discuss specifics after President Vladimir Putin said the war was “heading to an end.” (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1999789/russia-ukraine-resume-strikes-as-truce-expires'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/live/2026/may/12/europe-defence-ukraine-russia-hungary-latest-news-updates'>Three-day ceasefire ends with fresh wave of Russian attacks on Ukraine – as it happened</a> - theguardian.com</li><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/russian-attacks-in-dnipropetrovsk-region-kill-six-after-ceasefire-expires-officials-say'>Russian attacks in Dnipropetrovsk region kill six after ceasefire expires, officials say</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1999789/russia-ukraine-resume-strikes-as-truce-expires'>Russia, Ukraine resume strikes as